  "answer": "**Final status: passed.** The second verification run (`20261021T141514Z-497c5f`) passed all three configured stages: build, unit and component. It took one fix cycle.\n\n**What failed:** On the first run (`20261021T135228Z-886063`), the build passed but the unit stage failed and the run stopped there, so component tests never ran. One test failed on both net9.0 and net10.0: `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`. It expected the text `<absent>` in the failure output but got `expected: <not present>`.\n\n**Root cause:** The code had the wrong label. When a field is in the actual response but not in the expected body, `DeltaFormatter` printed `<not present>`. The project docs (`doc/failure-output.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, the skills' `writing-tests.md`) all specify `<absent>`, so the test was right and the code was wrong.\n\n**What was changed:** One line, `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`: `TestColor.Subtle(\"<not present>\")` became `TestColor.Subtle(\"<absent>\")`. Nothing else was edited.\n\nThe checks only run build, unit and component. Integration tests and the `make skills` check from `make ci` weren't part of this run. Nothing was committed.",
